<title>SWEDEN: Trucker strike to hit Saab mid-week.</title>
<headline>Trucker strike to hit Saab mid-week.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish carmaker Saab Automobile AB said on Thursday production would be stopped in the middle of next week if the French truckers' strike were not resolved before then.</p>
<p>&quot;In the middle of next week we will be forced to stop production if the French strike is not resolved. It is primarily because of a shortage of our Spanish-made cables,&quot; Saab Auto spokesman Olle Axelsson told Reuters.</p>
<p>A production stop would affect the 900 and the 9000 series.</p>
<p>&quot;If the strike is resolved at the last minute, we will fly spares to our plants to avoid stopping production. We did this in connection with the Norwegian strike in the spring,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Henrik Alberius, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1250</p>
